# LeakSanitizer suppressions for XIVO leak runs.
#
# Only third-party one-time allocations belong here. Every entry needs a reason;
# if a suppression is hiding XIVO's own allocation, that is a bug to fix, not to
# suppress. Match strings are checked against the symbolized stack frames, so
# `leak:<substring>` suppresses any leak whose stack mentions that substring.
#
# Used by scripts/mem/leakcheck.sh via LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...

# glog installs its own singletons (LogMessage internals, vmodule list, the
# LogDestination per severity) that it intentionally never frees; it has no
# shutdown API that releases them.
leak:google::LogMessage
leak:google::InitGoogleLogging
leak:google::LogDestination

# gflags keeps its registered-flag registry alive for the life of the process.
leak:gflags::

# OpenCV's lazily-created singletons: the thread pool / TLS storage, the
# algorithm registry and the ipp/ocl state. Created once, freed never.
leak:cv::TLSDataContainer
leak:cv::getThreadID
leak:cv::ThreadID
leak:cv::ocl::

# CPython interning, module state, and the pymalloc arenas are still reachable
# at interpreter exit when a C extension is loaded; relevant to the pyxivo
# runs only.
leak:_PyObject_GC_
leak:_PyMem_
leak:PyObject_Malloc
leak:PyType_Ready
leak:PyUnicode_
leak:_PyRuntimeState_Init
leak:pybind11::
leak:libpython3
